\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Initializes the receiver, a newly allocated NSCustomImageRep instance, so that it delegates responsibility for rendering the image to \i anObject\i0 . When the NSCustomImageRep receives a \b draw\b0  message, it will in turn send a message to \i anObject\i0  to perform the \i aMethod\i0  method. The \i aMethod\i0  method should take only one argument, the \b id\b0  of the NSCustomImageRep. It should draw the image at location (0.0,\'800.0) in the current coordinate system.\
